# Build output (root-anchored so cmd/forge/ and cmd/forge-agent/ are NOT ignored)
#
# There is no /forge line any more: the core package now sits there, and the
# pattern would have ignored it wholesale. Nothing is lost — the stray binary it
# covered came from `go build ./cmd/forge` in the repo root, which today refuses
# to write over a directory of that name. `make` puts binaries in bin/ regardless.
/bin/
/dist/
/forge-agent
*.exe

# Agent binaries copied in only during `make release` (embedded, never committed)
/internal/agentbin/forge-agent-linux-*

# Local runtime state (never committed)
/.forge/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
